PART 3c  the REDUCED tower (R_j): order j divided by H^(a-(j-1)b-1)
   (R_1)  c a Jac(H,Q_(m-1)) + c' b Jac(P_(n-1),H)/H^(a-b-... ) = 0
   (R_2)  c a H^b Jac(H,Q_(m-2)) + Jac(P_(n-1),Q_(m-1))/H^(a-b-1)
            + c' b Jac(P_(n-2),H)/H^(a-2b) = 0
   every term is a form of degree j(m-1)+g-2; valid for
   1 <= j <= floor((a-1)/b)+1  (= the first partial quotient of a/b).
